cff-version: 0.1.0-alpha
message: "If you use Q2D in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Q2D — a Fortran solver for 2D planar, 2D axisymmetric, and quasi-2D area-variation compressible flows"
abstract: >
  Q2D is an open-source CFD solver for compressible Euler and
  Navier–Stokes equations in three geometric regimes: 2D planar, 2D
  axisymmetric, and quasi-2D area-variation. It is part of the
  `open-hydra` release together with the companion 3D solver MOSE.
  Q2D supports inviscid and viscous flows, multi-species chemistry
  (CEA / finite-rate), one- and two-equation and Reynolds-stress transport RANS closures (Spalart–Allmaras,
  k–ω SST, k–ω Wilcox 2006, SSG/LRR), soot transport, surface chemistry,
  Borda-flow sudden-expansion injection (Fievisohn 2016/2017).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Montanari
    given-names: Alessandro
    email: alessandro.montanari@uniroma1.it
    affiliation: "Sapienza University of Rome (DIMA)"
license: GPL-3.0
url: "https://github.com/open-hydra/Q2D"
repository-code: "https://github.com/open-hydra/Q2D"
keywords:
  - "computational fluid dynamics"
  - "compressible flow"
  - "axisymmetric flow"
  - "quasi-2D"
  - "Fortran"
  - "RANS"
